  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced Opportunities for the Returning Migrants in Georgia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Georgia has experienced complex migration dynamics in the last three decades which includes an increasing number of migrants returning with greater vulnerabilities to social and economic exclusion. Returnees struggle with socio-economic reintegration, especially after a short and irregular migration. Several factors affect returnees&#x2019; prospects of sustainable reintegration, including availability and accessibility of infrastructure and services as well as access to information on available opportunities. The Government of Georgia has made reintegration of returning citizens a key priority of the Migration Strategy of Georgia and since 2015 has been allocating special funds from the state budget for supporting return Georgian migrants. The strategy acknowledges this issue and envisages programmes to support return migrants&#x2019; reintegration. The goal of the project is to design, test, synthesize and put forward a comprehensive model of reintegration of return migrants at the individual, community, and structural levels. The project will analyse different types of interventions and suggest the most effective and targeted model that results in the best reintegration outcomes. The results of this project will be used to develop the implementation strategy for the larger four-year on sustainable reintegration project in line with the long-term outlook of the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation.</narrative>
  </description>
